What Fixes Are Needed (Without Any Code Change Right Now)
Fix for Issue 1 (the stream error):In the Triage agent's chatbot node (and ALL other agents), instead of passing the full state["messages"], filter the messages before sending to LLM — strip out orphaned tool messages that don't have a preceding tool_calls message, OR only pass the last clean HumanMessage forward. This is a change only in the individual agent graph.py files.
Fix for Issue 2a (data silo):When POST /api/claims runs (Express route at line 114), it should also insert a corresponding record into claims_master so the frontend sees agent-created claims.
Fix for Issue 2b (approval body mismatch):Either the decision_router.py should add coverageStatus: "Confirmed" in the payload it sends, OR the Express route should default coverageStatus to "Confirmed" when called from the agent path (since the agent has already done coverage verification via Guidewire before calling approve).
Fix for Issue 2c (approval visibility):The PATCH /api/claims/:id route already syncs to claims_master for certain statuses. When approve_claim is called, it needs to also update the claims table row — which it does via storage.updateClaim(claimId, { status: "Approved" }) at line 3137, but only if claimId is passed. The agent doesn't pass claimId (only claimNumber), so the claims table never gets updated.
